      "topic_id": "bearings_cosine_rule",
      "prompt": "A ship sails from port A on a bearing of 224° for 26 km to point B. It then changes course and sails on a bearing of 144° for 15 km to point C. Find the direct distance from A to C, correct to 3 significant figures.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "The back bearing of A from B is 224° + 180° = 044°.",
        "Angle ABC is the difference between this back bearing and the bearing of C from B: angle ABC = 100°.",
        "Use the cosine rule: AC² = AB² + BC² - 2×AB×BC×cos(ABC)",
        "AC² = 26² + 15² - 2×26×15×cos(100°) = 1036",
        "AC = √1036 = 32.2 km (3 s.f.)"
      ],
      "final_answer": "32.2 km",
      "marks": 5,
      "mark_scheme": [
        {
          "code": "M1",
          "description": "The back bearing of A from B is 224° + 180° = 044°.",
